  "lifestyle": "Lifestyle",
  "healthyFeedingContent": "Providing a balanced and nutritious diet is critical for your dog's health. Choose quality food appropriate for their age, weight, and activity level. Feed 2-3 meals daily and always keep fresh water available. Avoid human foods, especially chocolate, grapes, and onions.",
  "catHappinessContent": "A happy cat needs play, scratching, and personal space. Play for at least 15 minutes daily. Create window sunbathing spots. Provide scratching posts and high platforms. Keep the litter box clean and create a calm environment.",
  "birdTrainingContent": "Patience and consistency are crucial when training your bird. Use positive reinforcement methods. Have short training sessions daily at the same time. Start with simple commands: step up, come when called. Use favorite treats as rewards. Watch for stress signs.",
  "smallPetHabitatContent": "Create an appropriately sized, clean, and safe living space for small pets. Ensure proper ventilation, natural light, and appropriate temperature. Add play and exercise areas. Provide hiding spots and nesting materials. Clean the cage at least weekly.",
  "commonDiseaseSymptomsContent": "Be alert if your pet shows loss of appetite, lethargy, vomiting, diarrhea, or behavior changes. Frequent urination, changes in drinking habits, or breathing difficulties are important signs. If you notice any of these symptoms, consult your vet immediately.",
  "travelingWithPetsContent": "When traveling with your pet, first get a health certificate from your vet. Get them used to the carrier at home before traveling. Take regular breaks on long journeys. Keep adequate water and food. Keep ID and microchip information updated. Check pet policies at your destination beforehand.",
